# wasm-pack output, produced by `just build-wasm` locally and by
# .github/workflows/publish-npm.yml at publish time. Never committed:
# regenerate it instead of pulling it from git.
#
# package.json is NOT here -- it is hand-maintained and holds the npm
# name and version, which is why the build copies individual artifacts in
# rather than `cp -r pkg/*`. That copy is what once overwrote this file
# with wasm-pack's own `*`, which silently untracked the whole directory.
fcb_wasm.js
fcb_wasm.d.ts
fcb_wasm_bg.wasm
fcb_wasm_bg.wasm.d.ts
snippets/

node_modules/
package-lock.json
